        "name": "v1.1.0 - Debatr: debates to videos 🎬",
        "draft": false,
        "immutable": false,
        "prerelease": false,
        "created_at": "2026-10-16T17:12:59Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-10-16T17:51:51Z",
        "published_at": "2026-10-16T17:51:51Z",
        "assets": [],
        "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/khoren93/debatr/tarball/v1.1.0",
        "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/khoren93/debatr/zipball/v1.1.0",
        "body": "### 🎬 AI Debates is now **Debatr**: from a live debate to a finished video\n\nA full redesign of the studio and a big step from \"watch models argue\" to \"turn the argument into content you can share\".\n\n**✨ Highlights**\n\n* **New studio UI**: dark Debatr theme, a four-step wizard (topic, speakers, voices & format, review) with the exact cost and length before you start, drafts and remixes.\n* **Smarter model picking**: searchable OpenRouter catalogue with provider logos, prices, leaderboard rank and a \"Latest\" filter; free models via `openrouter/free` out of the box.\n* **🧑‍⚖️ AI judge**: a structured verdict with the winner (or a draw), a headline and feedback for every debater.\n* **🔊 Voices**: premium ElevenLabs voices (v3, emotion tags, word timestamps) or free Edge voices, a karaoke-style transcript player and an MP3 of the whole debate.\n* **📹 Video in the browser**: a 16:9 episode plus a 9:16 Short cut around the strongest moments, rendered with Remotion right in your browser. No server-side encoding.\n* **👤 Accounts & credits**: sign up, keep a library of your debates, top up a prepaid balance with Stripe, or bring your own OpenRouter / ElevenLabs keys and run at your own cost.\n* **🖼️ Public gallery**: finished debates go public with a share link after an automatic content check (or stay private). Trending, New and Top for the week, month or year.\n* **🗳️ Engagement**: likes, a **blind audience vote** (you pick a winner before seeing the judge's call) and a **model leaderboard** with Bradley–Terry / Elo-style ratings built from those votes.\n* **🛡️ Admin panel**: moderation queue with approve / reject, users, ledger and debate management.\n\n**🐳 Self-hosting**\n\n* One `make up` (`docker compose up -d --build`) starts Postgres, Redis, API, debate and media workers and the Caddy-served frontend; migrations run automatically.\n* New `Makefile` shortcuts for dev, checks and deployment; `make check` runs everything CI does.\n* Backend moved to Python 3.12 + uv, async SQLAlchemy 2 + Alembic; frontend to React 19, Vite 8 and Tailwind 4.\n\n**⚠️ Upgrading from 1.0.0**\n\n* Copy the new variables from `.env.example` (`SECRET_KEY`, `ADMIN_*`, credits & payments, ElevenLabs, media settings) into your `.env`, and drop `DATABASE_URL` / `REDIS_URL`: Docker Compose now injects them.\n* Migrations apply on API start. Debates created before accounts stay readable via their link and are manageable from the admin panel.\n\n👉 See the [README](https://github.com/khoren93/debatr#readme) for setup instructions.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/khoren93/debatr/compare/v1.0.0...v1.1.0\n",
        "short_description_html": "<h3>🎬 AI Debates is now <strong>Debatr</strong>: from a live debate to a finished video</h3>\n<p>A full redesign of the studio and a big step from \"watch models argue\" to \"turn the argument into content you can share\".</p>\n<p><strong>✨ Highli…</strong></p>",
